{
  "note": "This decoder against a prototype cartridge that predates the compression. Offsets, lengths and digests only. No byte of either cartridge is recorded here and none can be recovered from this.",
  "why": "Every other witness for this decoder is downstream of the same reverse engineering, or is an encoder written by somebody modifying the game. This one is neither. Capcom shipped a prototype of the Japanese cartridge on 1996-09-15 that declares no coprocessor and stores data the retail cartridge compresses. Where a stream this decoder expands appears verbatim in that prototype, the bytes are Capcom's own input to Capcom's own compressor, so the decoder has been shown to invert it rather than to agree with somebody's reimplementation of it.",
  "rung": 2,
  "aboutTheRung": "The artifact itself, which is the second rung of the family ladder and the highest any question about this chip has reached. It is not a document, so it cannot say what the hardware is specified to do; it is evidence about what the data actually was.",
  "measuredOn": "2026-08-31",
  "howToRepeat": "Decompress every stream in the Japanese table from the retail cartridge and search the prototype image for the result. Neither image is carried here; both are identified below by four digests.",
